    "source_argument": [
      "Reset clears EX valid flags. A live eligible Load releases its EX slot in both normal/fault and blocked/retry branches.",
      "Recovery removes killed EX entries; fault and exit transitions clear EX slots. These paths admit no new instructions.",
      "The unchanged scheduler admits at most two MEM operations per cycle, so new Load occupancy cannot exceed two. The prototype asserts the live-load bound and requires each eligible Load to clear its source EX slot."
    ],
    "limitation": "The reachable-state bound is supported by source induction reasoning, per-cycle assertions and the listed reset-to-exit tests; no whole-core unbounded formal reachability proof was performed."
  },
